<section class="wrap max-w-3xl pt-16 sm:pt-24">
  <p class="eyebrow">Enterprise</p>
  <h1 class="h-page mt-4">Enterprise plan: $0</h1>
  <p class="lede">Includes the same software as the free plan, because there is only one.</p>
  <p class="mt-6 rounded-2xl bg-cream px-5 py-4 text-sm text-ink">
    Infloww's enterprise page cites "$2.61 billion USD in revenue generated in 2024 by Infloww users"
    (infloww.com/onlyfans-crm-enterprise, page stamped Oct 10, 2026). We don't publish a revenue figure for our
    users, and their 24/7 support and dedicated account managers have no equivalent here.
  </p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="who" class="wrap mt-16 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 id="who" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">Who this is for</h2>
  <div class="prose mt-4">
    <p>
      The README describes the project as an independent reverse-engineering of OnlyFans' public web API for personal /
      educational use. Nothing here is sold, and there is no enterprise contract. An agency can run it, but tell your
      creators before you connect theirs.
    </p>
    <p>{% include "tos.njk" %}</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="hosting" class="wrap mt-16 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 id="hosting" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">Self-hosting</h2>
  <div class="prose mt-4">
    <p>
      Inflowwww runs with Docker Compose on a server you control: a Python relay (FastAPI) that holds the captured
      sessions, a Next.js dashboard, and an autoheal container. The install is the
      <a href="{{ '/help/' | url }}">Quick start</a> from the README. The relay and the app bind to 127.0.0.1 on the host,
      and the app also joins the external <code>n8n_default</code> network with Traefik labels; if you run Traefik on
      that network it will be published. Otherwise making it reachable is a step you choose: a reverse proxy in front
      of the app, or the optional Cloudflare quick tunnel profile. Put local edits in a
      <code>docker-compose.override.yml</code> (the repository ignores it), not in the tracked file.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="backups" class="wrap mt-16 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 id="backups" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">Your backups</h2>
  <div class="prose mt-4">
    <p>
      Everything that matters is on the host: <code>service/chatterly.db</code> (SQLite), <code>service/sessions/</code>,
      <code>service/proxies.json</code>, <code>service/secrets/</code> and <code>.env</code>, plus the vault image folders
      (<code>service/vault_thumbs/</code>, <code>vault_posters/</code>, <code>vault_images/</code>), which can't be
      downloaded again once OnlyFans' signed URLs expire. The <code>service/</code> ones are bind-mounted into the relay;
      Compose reads <code>.env</code>. Back them up on your schedule, to your storage, and keep the copies as private as passwords:
      <code>chatterly.db</code> and <code>proxies.json</code> hold passwords in plain text. 
      <a href="{{ '/help/#backups' | url }}">Help &gt; Backups</a> has the backup commands and a restore test.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="proxies" class="wrap mt-16 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 id="proxies" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">Your proxies</h2>
  <div class="prose mt-4">
    <p>
      You choose the proxy provider and assign one per creator in Creators &gt; Custom proxy (<code>/creators/proxy</code>).
      The registry is <code>service/proxies.json</code> on your server.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="lock-in" class="wrap mt-16 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 id="lock-in" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">No vendor lock-in</h2>
  <div class="prose mt-4">
    <ul>
      <li>The data is one SQLite file you can open with any SQLite client.</li>
      <li>The code is one MIT-licensed repository (the project's source folder). Fork it, change it, and keep running your fork.</li>
      <li>There is no account with us, no licence key and no contract to end.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

